WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.900
We are going to put everything together

00:00:01.900 --> 00:00:04.920
for our full adult CPR scenario.

00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:07.200
This is where you practice the complete path

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:09.240
from the first moment of an emergency

00:00:09.240 --> 00:00:11.460
until professional help arrives.

00:00:11.460 --> 00:00:14.760
In small groups, your instructor will assign clear roles

00:00:14.760 --> 00:00:17.160
so everyone knows their responsibility.

00:00:17.160 --> 00:00:19.400
One person will be rescuer one,

00:00:19.400 --> 00:00:22.920
focusing on giving breaths and operating the AED.

00:00:22.920 --> 00:00:26.600
Rescuer two will handle those critical chest compressions.

00:00:26.600 --> 00:00:28.320
If you have a third person,

00:00:28.360 --> 00:00:31.760
they can take over as the dedicated AED operator.

00:00:31.760 --> 00:00:33.759
We want every person in the group

00:00:33.759 --> 00:00:35.700
to rotate through each role

00:00:35.700 --> 00:00:37.720
so you leave here feeling confident

00:00:37.720 --> 00:00:39.959
in every part of the rescue.

00:00:39.959 --> 00:00:41.220
Your instructor might choose

00:00:41.220 --> 00:00:43.520
to have multiple groups going at once,

00:00:43.520 --> 00:00:46.599
so don't be surprised if the room feels a bit loud.

00:00:46.599 --> 00:00:49.520
We do this on purpose because a real world emergency

00:00:49.520 --> 00:00:52.439
is rarely a quiet or calm place.

00:00:52.439 --> 00:00:54.000
After the scenario is complete,

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:56.160
your instructor will discuss performances

00:00:56.160 --> 00:00:57.840
and provide feedback.

00:00:57.840 --> 00:01:00.139
They may also choose to do a repeat scenario

00:01:00.139 --> 00:01:01.639
for additional practice.

